# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HOW TO EDIT THIS FILE
#
# A pattern without a leading slash matches at EVERY depth. `runs/` does not
# mean "the runs directory at the repo root", it means "any directory named
# runs, anywhere" -- which is exactly how an earlier version of this file
# silently excluded all 40 override files in configs/runs/.
#
# Rule used below:
#   - Tool-generated names that could never be study content (__pycache__,
#     .pytest_cache, .venv) stay UNANCHORED on purpose. They should be ignored
#     wherever they turn up.
#   - Ordinary English words that could plausibly name a real directory
#     (runs, outputs, data, corpus, results, checkpoints) are ANCHORED with a
#     leading slash, so they can only match at the repo root.
#
# Re-run the audit after any change here. Output from this command is a bug:
#   git check-ignore -v configs/base.yaml configs/runs/seed03_coherent.yaml \
#                       configs/burst_texts/coherent.txt
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Python, tool-generated. Unanchored deliberately.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/

# Virtual environments at the repo root. `venv` is an ordinary word, so it is
# anchored -- an unanchored `venv/` would also swallow e.g. configs/venv/.
/venv/
/env/

# The separate environment holding torch and transformers for
# scripts/burst_match.py. It is kept apart from .venv on purpose, so that the
# config test suite can be proved to still pass with no ML stack installed.
# `.venv/` above does not match this name.
/.venv-ml/

# The cached OpenWebText slice that scripts/make_bursts.py cuts spans from.
# Corpus data is never committed -- the corpus is named in the config, never
# vendored. The burst texts cut FROM it are committed, because those are
# experimental content rather than data; see bursts/ and CLAUDE.md.
/.corpus-cache/

# Run outputs. The provenance record that matters (resolved_config.yaml and
# run_provenance.yaml) is written into --outdir, which is chosen per machine
# and deliberately not tracked here.
/runs/
/outputs/
/results/
/checkpoints/

# Corpus and tokenized data. The corpus is NAMED in the config, never located
# in it, and never stored in the repo.
/data/
/corpus/

# Model weights, optimizer state and tokenized shards, wherever they land.
# Extensions rather than directory names, on purpose: --outdir can point
# anywhere, and a ~1.5 GB checkpoint must not be committable by accident.
#
# Note what is NOT here: *.txt. The burst texts are .txt and MUST be tracked --
# the whole point of injection.burst_text_paths is that the commit hash covers
# them. Do not add a *.txt rule.
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.npy
*.npz
*.arrow
*.h5

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
